@startuml
title D2 — Surefyre Product Architecture
caption How submissions move through Surefyre and connect to enterprise systems

left to right direction

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam wrapWidth 220
skinparam maxMessageSize 140
skinparam nodesep 85
skinparam ranksep 95
skinparam padding 20

skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 14
  BorderThickness 1.4
}
skinparam package {
  RoundCorner 16
  BorderThickness 1.8
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF8D6
  BorderColor #C8A84E
}

actor "Retail Agent /\nAgency User" as Agent

package "SUREFYRE PLATFORM" as Surefyre #EAF4EA {
  rectangle "Agent Portal\n\nExternal entry point for:\n• new submissions\n• document uploads\n• status and messages" as Portal #EAF2FF

  rectangle "Rules and Workflow Engine\n\n• field validation\n• completeness checks\n• eligibility checks\n• routing and referrals\n• task creation" as Rules #F3F8E8

  rectangle "Underwriting Workbench\n\nInternal workspace for:\n• review and analysis\n• requests for information\n• rating and quoting\n• decisions and referrals\n• activity and notes" as Workbench #EAF2FF

  Portal -right-> Rules : 1. Submit and validate
  Rules -right-> Workbench : 2. Route work
}

rectangle "AIM\n\nCore insurance operations\nand transaction data" as AIM #FFF1DF
rectangle "ImageRight\n\nDocuments, correspondence\nand workflow references" as ImageRight #FFF1DF
rectangle "Carrier / Rating /\nThird-Party Services\n\nExternal rates, decisions\nand enrichment data" as External #FFF1DF

Agent -right-> Portal : New submission,\ndocuments and messages

' Keep downstream systems vertically separated.
AIM -[hidden]down-> ImageRight
ImageRight -[hidden]down-> External

' Use dedicated interface points so labels and arrows remain separated.
circle " " as AOut
circle " " as AIn
circle " " as IOut
circle " " as IIn
circle " " as EOut
circle " " as EIn

Workbench -right-> AOut
AOut -right-> AIM : 3. Transaction and\npolicy data
AIM -left-> AIn : 4. Status and\nresults
AIn -left-> Workbench

Workbench -right-> IOut
IOut -right-> ImageRight : 5. Document metadata\nand requests
ImageRight -left-> IIn : 6. Document IDs\nand status
IIn -left-> Workbench

Workbench -right-> EOut
EOut -right-> External : 7. Rating, inquiry or\npolicy request
External -left-> EIn : 8. Response,\ndecision or enrichment
EIn -left-> Workbench

Workbench -[dashed]left-> Portal : Status, requests,\nquote and documents
Portal -[dashed]left-> Agent : User-facing response

legend bottom
|= Component |= Primary purpose |
| Agent Portal | External submission and communication |
| Rules and Workflow Engine | Validation, eligibility, routing, referrals and tasks |
| Underwriting Workbench | Internal review, rating, quoting and decisions |
| AIM | Core insurance operations and transaction processing |
| ImageRight | Insurance document and workflow management |
| Carrier / Rating / Third-Party Services | External rating, policy and data services |
endlegend

note bottom of Surefyre
Simplified interview model.
Exact system-of-record ownership, message direction,
and integration behavior should be confirmed with SPG.
end note

@enduml
